# operator_project.skill — CDLC Context Package
# KQLBridge v0.1 | Generate → Test → Distribute → Observe
# ============================================================

## What project does in KQL
Selects a specific subset of columns, projecting them forward in the pipe.
Drops all columns not listed. Analogous to SELECT col1, col2 in SQL.

## Translation table
| KQL                              | Spark SQL                         |
|----------------------------------|-----------------------------------|
| T | project a, b, c              | SELECT a, b, c FROM T             |
| T | project a | summarize count() | SELECT COUNT(*) FROM (SELECT a FROM T) |

## Full examples
```kql
Heartbeat | project Computer, TimeGenerated, Category
```
```sql
SELECT Computer, TimeGenerated, Category
FROM Heartbeat
```

## Edge cases
- project after where: WHERE is applied first, SELECT uses projected cols
- project before summarize: summarize still works on the projected cols
- Quoted column names: KQL allows `project ["odd column"]` — not supported in v0.1

## Known limits
- v0.1 does NOT support `project-away` or `project-rename`
- Column rename in project (`project newname = oldcol`) → v0.2 roadmap

## Routing rules
- project_op → SUPPORTED → SparkSQLGenerator._project()
- `project-away` keyword → UNSUPPORTED → raise UnsupportedOperatorError
